{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Spaceship engine room (loop)",
  "description": "The engine room of an old long-haul freighter under way: the reactor core throbs once every two seconds, a deep unstable tone that never quite repeats, the plasma conduits sing a slow swirling chord above it, coolant hisses through the pipes, and a status panel pings to itself in the corner. Steel walls, a tank of a room. An 8 s stereo loop; the throb and the swirl are tied to the loop length (0.5 and 0.125 Hz) and the seam is crossfaded over 1 s.",
